        "answer": {
          "short": "Decreasing at $\\dfrac{50}{9\\pi}\\text{ cm/s}$.",
          "worked": "First find the radius:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac43\\pi r^3&=36\\pi\\\\r^3&=27\\\\r&=3\\text{ cm}.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $\\dfrac{dV}{dt}=-200\\text{ cm}^3/\\text{s}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}-200&=4\\pi(3)^2\\frac{dr}{dt}\\\\\\frac{dr}{dt}&=-\\frac{200}{36\\pi}\\\\\\frac{dr}{dt}&=-\\frac{50}{9\\pi}\\text{ cm/s}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe radius is decreasing at $\\dfrac{50}{9\\pi}\\text{ cm/s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
